nodecode-microbiz-desk is a rewrite of Danzilla0's Danzilla0/microbiz-desk:

  https://github.com/Danzilla0/microbiz-desk
  commit c737d9e4d73a5eeb6995408a0e10fb50a60ce7aa
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Daniel Wisdom (LICENSE)

Rewritten in Common Lisp against Nodecode's cell contract: the five tools
keep their names, arguments and JSON answers, the money kept in whole
minor units so totals never drift, the customer lookup that accepts a partial
name only when exactly one customer matches, the refusal of an overpayment and
of a payment from someone who owes nothing, and the words of the debt list,
the statement and the weekly report. The original's SQLite database is one
JSON file in a folder the section names, guarded by that folder's lock; its
`hermes microbiz ...` CLI subcommand and its `/microbiz` command are one
`/microbiz-desk` slash command, since a cell's command is its own. Left out:
nothing of what a user does -- every tool, every command and every figure is
here. The envelope is different: the original read HERMES_HOME and could be
pointed at another database with MICROBIZ_DB, where this names its folder in
the cell's section.
